   - `exit_status_for()` recomputes the status rather than trusting the stored one, so
     post-construction mutation or a subclass cannot produce a green exit.
   - The rendering fallback leads with a documented code, `GATE_DIAGNOSTIC_UNRENDERABLE`, so the
     stderr contract holds even there.
   - Real `GateFailure`s still pass through unchanged, so `PLAN_FINGERPRINT_PENDING` and real
     mismatch detail survive.

